        "content": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\ntypedef long long ll;\n\nint A[1000][1000];\n\nll solve(int m, int n, int k) {\n  const int paired = min(m, n);\n  const int length = max(m, n);\n  const bool transpose = m > n;\n  unique_ptr<int[]> oriented;\n\n  if (transpose) {\n    oriented.reset(new int[static_cast<size_t>(paired) * length]);\n    const int tile = 32;\n    for (int i0 = 0; i0 < m; i0 += tile) {\n      const int i_end = min(m, i0 + tile);\n      for (int j0 = 0; j0 < n; j0 += tile) {\n        const int j_end = min(n, j0 + tile);\n        for (int j = j0; j < j_end; ++j) {\n          int* destination = oriented.get() + static_cast<size_t>(j) * length;\n          for (int i = i0; i < i_end; ++i)\n            destination[i] = A[i][j];\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  vector<int> band(length);\n  unordered_map<ll, ll> h;\n  ll ans = 0;\n\n  for (int first = 0; first < paired; ++first) {\n    fill(band.begin(), band.end(), 0);\n    for (int last = first; last < paired; ++last) {\n      const int* row = transpose\n          ? oriented.get() + static_cast<size_t>(last) * length\n          : A[last];\n\n      // Keep the contiguous update separate from hash-dependent counting.\n      for (int x = 0; x < length; ++x)\n        band[x] += row[x];\n\n      h.clear();\n      h[0] = 1;\n      ll s = 0;\n      for (int x = 0; x < length; ++x) {\n        s += band[x];\n        ans += h.find(s - k) != h.end() ? h[s - k] : 0;\n        h[s]++;\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  return ans;\n}\n\nint main() {\n  ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n  cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n  int k, m, n;\n  cin >> k >> m >> n;\n\n  for (int i = 0; i < m; i++)\n    for (int j = 0; j < n; j++)\n      cin >> A[i][j];\n\n  cout << solve(m, n, k) << endl;\n  return 0;\n}\n",
        "path": "src/main.cpp"
      }
    ],
    "hypothesis": "Contiguous incremental band sums, updated in a separate vectorizable pass, should improve locality over strided prefix accesses while retaining the reference frequency-counting kernel.",
